infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Tuning the lease timeout: a trap, not a fix
  desc Either way split-brain survives — only a fencing token removes it
  compares
    - label Long lease
      children
        - label Split-brain rarer
          desc A long timeout fits more pauses inside the lease
        - label Failover slow
          desc Cluster waits the full timeout before electing a new leader
        - label Split-brain still possible
          desc No timeout covers an arbitrarily long GC pause or partition
    - label Short lease
      children
        - label Failover fast
          desc Dead leader is replaced quickly
        - label Split-brain likelier
          desc A brief stall outlasts the lease and a frozen node wakes up "leader"
        - label Split-brain still possible
          desc No timeout tells "dead" from "frozen about to wake"
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
